### Quest Lines ###

## GT Steam Reborn

betterquesting.questline.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§6§lGT Steam Reborn
betterquesting.questline.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=A full steam-age expansion for GregTech: 22 steam multiblocks, the singularity tech chain, and a cross-dimensional hub-and-node logistics network.%n%nSeven chapters: steam basics, low-tier and large multiblocks, hub logistics, the singularity endgame, challenges, and the MIAO series beyond.%n%nSteam is all you need.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.name=§a§lGT Steam Reborn
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQ.desc=GT Steam Reborn bolts a full steam-age expansion onto GregTech: 22 steam multiblocks, a singularity tech chain, and a hub-and-node logistics network that reaches across chunks and dimensions.%n%nThis line walks the whole tree in seven chapters: steam basics, low-tier and large multiblocks, hub logistics, the singularity endgame, challenges, and a look at the wider MIAO series.%n%nSteam is all you need — no EU required until you feel like it.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.name=Bronze Age, ReSteamed
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAg.desc=GregTech already hands you bronze and steel steam machines in the Steam Age. GTSR builds on that foundation: its multiblocks drink the same steam your GT boilers make, from 1,000 L/s drills up to 24,000 L/s singularity hardware.%n%nKeep the bronze tier running while you gather steel — most GTSR multiblocks here have a bronze variant unless noted.%n%n§6Steam consumption in this line is quoted in L/s (liters per second).
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.name=A Field Guide to Steam
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAw.desc=Six grades of steam power GTSR: plain Steam, Superheated Steam and Supercritical Steam, each with a Dense variant — Dense Steam, Dense Superheated and Dense Supercritical.%n%nPlain grades come from GT boilers and GTSR producers; superheated steam is what the gear-driven compressor and the chipped geothermal boiler put out; dense variants are 1,000:1 compressed by the Dense State Manipulator; supercritical grades feed the singularity machines.%n%nSuperheated steam runs steam-base multiblocks at 4x speed for 4x the steam — even on bronze tier.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.name=It Came From the Sky
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABA.desc=Runaway Singularities spawn naturally on the surface of the Overworld and the Nether — about one per 48x48 chunks by default. They look like white animated spheres with a reach of 8-16 blocks.%n%nThe natural kind (attribute 'nature') has hardness 4: punch it by hand and it pops with a visual blast that drops 0-1 Steam Entangled Singularities — no real block damage.%n%nAn easy early source of your first singularity, if you don't mind the hike.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.name=Your First Entanglement
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABQ.desc=Time to hold one. The Steam Entangled Singularity is the currency of GTSR: chips, remote nodes, hub bindings and singularity machines all cost them.%n%nGet it from a natural runaway singularity, a structure chest, or — later — the Steam Singularity Entangler in chapter 5.%n%nFair warning: dropped singularities explode after 5 seconds (no block damage). Keep them in your inventory, not on the floor.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.name=Loot Box Lottery
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABg.desc=Six kinds of structure chests — village, dungeon, mineshaft, stronghold and friends — carry a Steam Entangled Singularity at roughly 2%% per chest.%n%nOptional: hand in two more singularities if your looting went well. No pressure — this one never blocks the line.%n%nThe real factory arrives in chapter 5.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.name=Superheated and Supersized
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAABw.desc=The single most important speed rule: feed a steam-base multiblock superheated steam and it runs at 4x speed while drinking 4x the steam. Works on bronze tier too — there is no tier gate.%n%nExceptions worth memorizing: the Siemens-Martin Furnace requires superheated steam outright; the Singularity Drilling Hub requires it but gets NO speedup; the Kinetic Processing Array is superheated-only by design.%n%nMake superheated steam with the Gear Steam Compressor (chapter 3) or a chipped geothermal boiler.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.name=Condensation Education
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACA.desc=Steam comes back as water, mostly. Plain steam spent in steam-base machines condenses into coolant water at 160 steam : 1 water; superheated steam cools 1:1 back into plain steam and lands in pressure cooling hatches.%n%nDense State Manipulator decompression (1:1000) and mega turbines burning dense steam return distilled water. Boilers fed plain water calcify — distilled water is exempt.%n%nA distilled water hatch on your boiler loop saves the limescale headaches later.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.name=§6§lSteam Multiblocks I
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACQ.desc=Chapter two: the low-tier workhorse multiblocks. Nine machines cover smelting, coking, air, drilling, oil-vein and void-mining duty.%n%nThe Reinforced Brick Blast Furnace, Large Steam Furnace, Large Coke Oven, Air Compressor, Atmospheric Centrifuge, Steam Fluid Drill, Vein Steam Pyrolyzer, Siemens-Martin Furnace and Crust Steam Borer all live here.%n%nMachine quests are retrieval tasks: craft the controller once and show it to the quest book.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.name=Brick by Brick
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACg.desc=The Reinforced Brick Blast Furnace is your steel-age primer: a compact 3x3x5 (W×H×L) steel-only multiblock running the GT5U brick blast furnace recipe list.%n%nController recipe: GT5U brick blast furnace controller + 8 steel plates in a crafting grid. Firebrick top, solid steel casing middle, steel firebox bottom.%n%nFurnace heat rises +0.01%%/s while working; parallel slots scale with heat from 1 (cold) to 4 (100%%), recipe speed up to 1.5x. Idle it drops 1%%/s.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.name=Warm Front
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAACw.desc=Heat only changes speed and parallel — it never changes which recipes match. A cold furnace still runs your first steel batches at 1x with a single parallel slot.%n%nEach 1%% of furnace heat adds +1%% recipe speed on top of the base, and parallel slots follow 1 + 3×heat (rounded): 25%% heat already gives you 2 slots.%n%nKeep the furnace fed continuously — every idle second throws away 1%% of heat.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.name=The Big Melt
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADA.desc=The Large Steam Furnace is a 5x5x5 parallel furnace running vanilla furnace recipes: 24 parallel on bronze, 48 on steel.%n%nStructure is casing + firebox + frame — at minimum one steam input hatch and one output bus. It applies an EU discount (bronze 0.6, steel 0.4) and a time modifier (0.4 / 0.2) to the recipe's EU cost before converting to steam.%n%nSuperheated steam: 4x speed for 4x steam. Your ore-smelting bottleneck days are over.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.name=Discount EU
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADQ.desc=How much steam is a recipe? Steam-base machines convert recipe EU/t into steam: steam(L/s) = EUt × 10,000 / max(1,000, efficiency).%n%nWith the furnace's EU discount applied first, a typical 8 EU/t smelt costs 8×0.6 = 4.8 effective EU/t on bronze — roughly 48,000 L/s across 24 parallels.%n%nTranslation: higher tier equals cheaper steam per operation. Steel pays off.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.name=Oven, Oversized
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADg.desc=The Large Coke Oven stacks the GT5U coke oven into a 3x7x7 (W×H×L) multiblock with heavy parallelism and a heat mechanic.%n%nIt runs the original GT5U coke oven recipes (Railcraft only): coal to coke + 500mB creosote, logs to charcoal, sugar cane to paper and more.%n%nBase speed is 120%% on bronze, 200%% on steel; each 1%% of oven heat adds another 1%% speed while running (+0.01%%/s) — a hot steel oven cooks coal in about 45 seconds.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.name=Creosote River
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAADw.desc=Optional delivery: dump 16 coal into the oven program. Every coal recipe yields 1 coke plus 500mB of creosote oil; coal blocks bake for a full 810 seconds base.%n%nCharcoal from logs only gives 250mB — reserve wood for when you need the charcoal itself.%n%nCreosote is your early fuel-oil and wood-treatment stock.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.name=Air Apparent
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEA.desc=The Air Compressor is a small 5x4x3 machine that turns steam straight into air: bronze makes 800 L/s for 400 L/s of steam; steel makes 3,200 L/s for 1,200 L/s.%n%nNo recipe lookup — it pumps air into its output hatch every 20-tick cycle, with 1 parallel on bronze and 4 on steel.%n%nThis is the feeder for the Atmospheric Centrifuge two doors down.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEQ.name=Hellish Air Quality
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEQ.desc=Build the compressor in the Nether (dimension -1) and its output flips to Nether Air automatically — same rates, different chemistry.%n%nNether air feeds the centrifuge's nether recipes: 10,000mB gives nitric oxide, sulfur dioxide and sulfur trioxide; the 100,000mB variant adds chlorine, neon, anthracene and radon.%n%nThe big nether batch needs the Rare Gas Separation Chip.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEg.name=Centrifugal Force of Nature
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEg.desc=The Atmospheric Centrifuge is a 7x4x7 machine that splits air into components: 10,000mB of air becomes 7,800mB nitrogen + 2,100mB oxygen.%n%n4 parallel on bronze, 16 on steel. Without a chip it only runs recipes with up to 3 fluid outputs.%n%nThe fluid grid GUI shows every output at once — nitrogen for the ammonia plant, oxygen for everything else.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.name=Rare Air
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEw.desc=The Rare Gas Separation Chip unlocks the centrifuge's rare-gas recipes — and locks the normal ones while installed.%n%nSteel tier only: on a bronze centrifuge the GUI just says 'steel tier required' and the chip does nothing.%n%nWith it, 2,000,000mB of air yields argon, carbon dioxide, neon, methane, krypton and helium on top of the nitrogen-oxygen base.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.name=Noble Gases, Ignoble Cost
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFA.desc=The full rare batch: 2,000,000mB air gives 1,560,000mB nitrogen, 420,000mB oxygen, 3,860mB argon, 600mB CO2, 40mB neon, 4mB methane, 2mB krypton and 1mB helium.%n%nAt 40,000 ticks base it is a long cook — the 4x superheated speedup matters here more than anywhere.%n%nNeon and krypton feed quantum-era recipes much later; stockpile shamelessly.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.name=Water Where You Want It
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFQ.desc=The Steam Fluid Drill is a 5x6x5 rig that pumps water straight from the ground: 200 to 2,000 L/s on bronze, 200 to 8,000 L/s on steel, for 1,000 L/s of steam.%n%nEfficiency climbs from zero with each completed cycle — bronze gains 33%% per cycle but caps low; steel gains 3%% per cycle but climbs to the 8,000 L/s ceiling.%n%nNeeds exactly one steam input hatch and one fluid output hatch.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.name=Screwdriver Sommelier
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFg.desc=Screwdriver-right-click the drill controller to cycle products: water → distilled water → brine → lava → water. Steel tier only; bronze stays locked to water.%n%nRates relative to water mode: distilled 20%%, brine 10%%, lava 0.5%% (5%% in the Nether). Brine and lava modes drink 4,000 L/s of steam instead of 1,000.%n%nMode switches reset efficiency to zero — plan your switches, not your impulses.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.name=Vein, Meet Steam
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFw.desc=The Vein Steam Pyrolyzer is a 7x7x7 tower that reaches into the underground oil system: on first run it locks onto the fluid beneath its chunk, then scans nearby chunks for the same fluid.%n%nEvery completed work cycle (360s bronze / 180s steel) it injects +10,000mB / +25,000mB into every matched chunk's reservoir — oil fields that refill themselves.%n%nSteam: 1,000 L/s bronze, 4,000 L/s steel.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.name=Chip Off the Old Vein
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGA.desc=The pyrolyzer's controller slot takes range chips. T1 widens the scan by +1 chunk per side: 1 chunk becomes a 2x2 (4 chunks).%n%nAssembler recipe, HV: an oil drill T2 controller + 16 singularities + 32 stainless double plates + 8 HV circuits, soldered with tin alloy.%n%nChips are install-and-forget — they widen the scan, nothing more.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.name=Scanline Expansion
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGQ.desc=The chip line tops out at T3: T1 scans 2x2 chunks, T2 4x4 (16), T3 8x8 (64). Each tier's recipe consumes the previous chip — they are upgrades, not collectibles.%n%nCosts scale like everything singularity-adjacent: 16, 32, 64 singularities for T1/T2/T3.%n%nA T3 pyrolyzer blankets a small ocean of oil chunks.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.name=Open Hearth, Closed System
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGg.desc=The Siemens-Martin Furnace is a giant 12x19x14 steel-only smelter that turns iron + carbon into steel: 2 iron + 2 coal → 2 steel is the base recipe.%n%nIt demands superheated steam — 6,000 L/s to warm up, falling as furnace heat climbs (3,000 L/s running hot, 1,500 L/s at 200%%).%n%nParallelism scales from 64 to 128 with furnace heat. Coke recipes (1,200s) and carbon dust recipes (800s, fastest) fill the list.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.name=Hotter Than 100%%
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAGw.desc=At 100%% furnace heat the SMF starts working. While running recipes it keeps gaining +0.01%%/s heat and breaks past 100%% — all the way to 200%%.%n%nEvery 1%% above 100%% cuts recipe time by 0.5%%, up to a 50%% cut at 200%%. When you stop, heat falls back at 1%%/s.%n%nKeep it always-on: a continuously fed SMF at 200%% runs at half recipe time and a quarter of the steam draw.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.name=Crust Fundamentals
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHA.desc=The Crust Steam Borer is your void miner on a budget: 9x11x9, 2,000 L/s of steam, one 500-tick (25s) cycle per random ore from the current dimension's drop table.%n%nWorks in the Overworld and the Nether; anywhere else it refuses to run. Superheated steam quarters the cycle to 125 ticks.%n%nIt's the little sibling of chapter 5's Crust Matter Aggregator — same idea, singularity-free.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.name=§5§lSteam Multiblocks II
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHQ.desc=Chapter three: the heavy industrial tier. Producers, converters, and the mega turbine that turns it all back into EU.%n%nThe Large Geothermal Steam Boiler, Large Solar Overpressure Array, Gear Steam Compressor, Ammonia Plant, Kinetic Processing Array and Mega Steam Turbine Array live here.%n%nThis is where steam becomes an economy.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.name=Magma Powered
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHg.desc=The Large Geothermal Steam Boiler drinks lava and breathes steam: 60,000 L/s on bronze, 150,000 L/s on steel, scaling with heat (output = max × heat%%).%n%nEach cycle consumes 1,000mB of lava with chances of byproducts — obsidian 20%%, ash 10%%, sulfur dust 8%% and more.%n%nCold start burns 333mB/s of lava; a hot steel boiler settles at 200mB/s. Overpressure mode (screwdriver, needs 100%% heat) doubles the ceiling to 200%% heat.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.name=Overheat Overclock
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAHw.desc=Drop a Geothermal Overheat Chip into the boiler's controller slot (steel tier only) and its output flips from plain steam to superheated steam.%n%nChip mode heats slower (0.004%%/s) with an 80-tick recipe cycle; hot-state lava draw rises to 250mB/s.%n%nAssembler recipe, LV: 6 singularities + 4 gold plates + 4 steel plates + 2 LV circuits + 8 LV pumps. Cheap for what it does.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.name=Obsidian Byproducts
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIA.desc=Every 1,000mB of lava has a chance to precipitate: obsidian 20%%, ash 10%%, sulfur dust 8%%, tantalite 4%%, alumina 6%%, copper 2%%, tin 1%%, silver 0.5%%, gold 0.35%%.%n%nWith the overheat chip three more rares join: phosphorus 0.1%%, rutile 0.05%%, scheelite 0.02%%.%n%nYour lava lake is now a strip mine. NEI shows both product lists as display recipes.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.name=Solar Farm, Steam Farm
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIQ.desc=The Large Solar Overpressure Array is a 30x27x7 mirror farm: 120,000 L/s steam on bronze, 180,000 on steel, 240,000 on the silver tier — and silver outputs superheated steam directly.%n%nThe steam-to-water ratio is 160:1. It only heats in daylight, under open sky, in clear weather.%n%nSolar booster items in the controller slot (bronze / HP solar boilers) add up to +200%% on the solar share; stacked with overpressure mode the total ceiling is 4x base output.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.name=Hard Water Problems
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIg.desc=Feed the array plain water and it calcifies — scale accumulates and chokes output, up to 100%% calcification (zero steam). The GUI has a manual descale button.%n%nDistilled water never calcifies. Same rules apply to the geothermal boiler's water side.%n%nRun out of water entirely and the machine hard-stops with a chat warning; a soft mallet or the GUI power switch restarts it.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.name=Four to One
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAIw.desc=The Gear Steam Compressor squeezes 4 steam into 1 superheated steam: bronze takes 6,400 L/s of steam and returns 1,600 L/s superheated + 30 L/s distilled water; steel does 25,600 → 6,400 + 120.%n%nRuns every tick, no recipe system. The whole structure must match a single tier — mixing bronze and steel parts never forms.%n%nThis is your superheated steam plant for the SMF, the Kinetic array and the Drilling Hub.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.name=Smells Like Ammonia
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJA.desc=The Ammonia Plant is a 10x14x13 steel-only factory: refinery gas + nitrogen → ammonia, with superheated steam as a byproduct.%n%nPreheat needs 8,000 L/s steam + 200 L/s refinery gas; running costs 12,000 L/s steam + 200 L/s refinery gas plus extra steam per parallel (parallel × 16,000 / reaction seconds).%n%nRecipes only run at 100%% heat — same warmup discipline as the SMF.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.name=Catalyst for Change
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJQ.desc=The plant's controller slot takes one of seven catalysts — they set parallelism and reaction time. Nickel is the entry: 64 parallel, 64 seconds per reaction.%n%nThe assembler recipes climb HV through platinum, uranium, osmium, iron-cobalt and ruthenium up to quantum at UV.%n%nReaction time is the real multiplier: shorter reactions mean more extra steam per second (parallel × 16,000 / seconds).
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJg.name=Platinum Plus Uranium
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJg.desc=Mid-grade catalysts: platinum runs 96 parallel at 48s, uranium 128 parallel at 64s. Both are EV-IV assembler jobs.%n%nHand in one of each — the plant only ever uses the installed one, so spares are trade goods.%n%nStill in the queue: osmium (192/24s), iron-cobalt (256/16s), ruthenium (256/8s) and quantum (256/1s).
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJw.name=Quantum Leap
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAJw.desc=The quantum catalyst tops the table: 256 parallel with 1-second reactions — up to 4,096,000 L/s of extra steam at full tilt.%n%nIts assembler recipe is UV tier with quantum and cosmic neutron dusts plus osmium dense plates, soldered in krypton.%n%nAt this point the ammonia plant stops being a chemistry set and becomes a superheated steam fountain.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKA.name=One Array, Any Recipe
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKA.desc=The Kinetic Processing Array is a 7x5x7 chassis that eats single-block GT machines: pop an electrolyzer, centrifuge, chemical reactor, mixer, packager, brewer or rock breaker into the controller slot and the array runs its recipe map at multiblock scale.%n%nSuperheated steam only. Parallelism = (1 + 2 × machine tier) + stack size, and the steam draw per recipe falls with machine tier (HV 1.0x, IV 0.5x, LuV 0.1x).%n%nBase package: 200%% speed, 40%% energy discount before steam conversion.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKQ.name=Pipe Dreams and Gears
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKQ.desc=The array's pipe column sets speed: steel 200%%, stainless 250%%, titanium 300%%. The gear column sets energy discount: steel 40%%, titanium 60%%.%n%nSteam consumption scales with the inserted machine's tier: ULV 8.0x down to LuV/ZPM 0.1x — a titanium array running HV machines is the sweet spot.%n%nThe machine you insert is never consumed; swap freely.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKg.name=Steam to EU, Mega-Sized
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKg.desc=The Mega Steam Turbine Array is your steam-to-EU converter: a 13x13 footprint, 9 to 25 blocks tall (base + up to 4 stack groups), 12 casing tiers from steel to space-time.%n%nEfficiency ceilings by steam grade: 150%% plain steam, 200%% superheated, 250%% supercritical, 300%% dense supercritical. Dense grades need tier 6+.%n%nSteam priority is automatic: dense supercritical > supercritical > dense superheated > dense > superheated > plain. Cooling products return as distilled water (or plain steam for superheated input).
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKw.name=Stack It Higher
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKw.desc=Each extra stack group adds +5%% steam savings and +10%% efficiency ceiling (additive). Advanced gears add +2.5%%/+5%%; titanium pipes +10%% ceiling, tungsten steel pipes +25%%.%n%nEvery casing tier above tier 1 adds another +5%% ceiling; singularity mode adds a flat +100%%.%n%nStack bonuses are why a fully-built high-tier turbine on tungsten steel pipes blows past 300%% efficiency.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALA.name=Dial Down the Watts
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALA.desc=Screwdriver-click the turbine controller to cycle the global power parameter: 10 → 8 → 6 → 4 → 2, shown as 100%% / 80%% / 60%% / 40%% / 20%%.%n%nThe parameter multiplies base EU/t directly and sets the base steam savings: 20%% / 15%% / 10%% / 5%% / 0%% respectively.%n%nThrottle down when your steam supply dips — a slower turbine wastes far less steam than a stalling one.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALQ.name=§2§lHubs and Logistics
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALQ.desc=Chapter four: the hub-and-node network — GTSR's answer to fluid logistics. Three hubs (steam, water, drilling) bind remote cache nodes across chunks and dimensions.%n%nBind by holding a node and right-clicking the hub controller. First bindings cost singularities: 0 plain / 1 reinforced / 8 overpressure; miner and driller nodes cost 1 each.%n%nEverything is managed from one handheld terminal.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALg.name=The Steam Backbone
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALg.desc=The Steam Hub Array is a 9x9 tower, 3 to 32 blocks tall: every stack layer adds 25 storage unit slots, up to 750 units at full height.%n%nCapacity per unit: 320M plain / 1.28G reinforced / 20.48G overpressure liters. The controller slot takes a Hub Singularity Chip — it enables node transfer and multiplies total capacity ×5.%n%nThe hub itself never consumes steam. Auto-output through steam hub output hatches runs at 20,000,000 L/s.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALw.name=Chip In
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAALw.desc=The Hub Singularity Chip is crafted in a plain crafting table: 8 GT pressed plates around the rim, any 2 LV circuits in the middle column, 1 Steam Entangled Singularity dead center.%n%nIt is mandatory for both cache hubs: no chip, no node transfers and no capacity multiplier.%n%nHand-carry one to every hub you build; hand one in here to prove the recipe.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMA.name=Cache Money
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMA.desc=The Steam Cache Node is a 16,000,000 L digital tank that auto-outputs 2,000,000 L/s through the face it points at — and binds to a steam hub for two-way transfer at the same rate.%n%nCrafting table: triple bronze plates + large bronze pipes around a ULV fluid tank core.%n%nBinding costs 0 singularities — the cheapest node in the family.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMQ.name=Reinforced Caching
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMQ.desc=The Reinforced Steam Cache Node quadruples everything: 64,000,000 L capacity, 8,000,000 L/s transfer and auto-output.%n%nUpgrade in a crafting table: triple steel plates + large steel pipes around your existing plain node.%n%nFirst binding to a hub costs 1 singularity. The overpressure tier (chapter 5 logistics) costs 8 and needs a tier-3 hub with the reinforced chip.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMg.name=Water Works
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMg.desc=The Water Hub Array is the universal-fluid hub: a 7x7 footprint, 2 to 31 tall, 9 storage slots per layer. It carries any single fluid at a time (type-locked once filled).%n%nUnit capacities: 1.28M / 5.12M / 20.48M liters on bronze / steel / tungsten steel tiers; the singularity chip multiplies ×5.%n%nAuto-output runs at 1,280,000 L/s. Bound fluid nodes interact at their own rates (64K to 2M per cycle).
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMw.name=Universal Fluid Nodes
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMw.desc=The fluid cache node family comes in three grades: 2M / 8M / 32M liters, interacting at 64,000 / 256,000 / 2,000,000 L per 20-tick cycle.%n%nEvery one of them binds for zero singularities — the friendliest binding economy in the mod.%n%nThey're digital tanks on their own: auto-output, no hub required. The overpressure grade still needs a tier-3 hub with the reinforced chip.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANA.name=The Compartment Quartet
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANA.desc=Four singularity compartments bolt into hub structures as hatches: the Singularity Steam Compartment (receives from the steam hub) and its output sibling (pushes into it), plus the fluid input/output pair for the water hub.%n%nThey're mode-locked — no input/output cycling, ever. Pipes cannot inject into them; only the hub link talks to them.%n%nFixed interaction rates: 8M L per cycle for the steam pair, 256K for the fluid pair. Binding costs: 1/1/0/0 singularities.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANQ.name=Compartments, Completed
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANQ.desc=Complete the set: hand in the steam output compartment and the fluid output compartment.%n%nOutput-side compartments push into their hub at fixed rates and refuse every other interaction — place them where the hub needs inflow.%n%nAll four build from assembler recipes (reworked in v1.10.84) — check NEI for the pairings.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANg.name=Storage, Stacked and Tiered
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANg.desc=Hub storage units are the hub's capacity cells: plain 320M liters (bronze hubs only), reinforced 1.28G (steel), overpressure 20.48G (tungsten steel).%n%nTier enforcement is strict: a steel hub only accepts reinforced units. A full-height steam hub holds 750 of them.%n%nThe reinforced chip on a tier-3 hub multiplies everything ×20 — that's 10.24 trillion liters on a full overpressure build.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANw.name=Terminal Velocity
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAANw.desc=The Hub Terminal is the remote control for the entire network: 1 singularity surrounded by 8 steel plates in a crafting table.%n%nRight-click any hub controller to open its status screen: every bound node listed with rate, capacity, mode, auto-output and rename controls, plus teleport.%n%nRight-click a cache node to cycle its transfer rate (100%% → 0%%); sneak-right-click toggles input/output mode. Empty-hand shift-click cycles capacity limits.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOA.name=Beam Me Up, Singularity
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOA.desc=The teleport button on any terminal row moves you to that node — cross-dimension included, with automatic chunk loading and safe-spot search.%n%nCost: exactly 1 Steam Entangled Singularity from your inventory, charged only after a safe landing spot is found. Failed search or empty wallet: no teleport, no charge.%n%nNo cooldown. Your mining outposts are now one click away.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOQ.name=Reinforce the Hub
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOQ.desc=The Reinforced Hub Singularity Chip is the tier-3 hub's license to do everything: node binding, dense and supercritical steam compatibility, ×20 capacity, and overpressure node binding.%n%nOnly works on tungsten steel hubs — lower tiers show a red 'higher tier required' warning.%n%nThe assembler recipe runs at LuV with a 384-singularity bill (six stacks of 64) plus dense europium and rhodium-plated palladium plates, soldered in radon. The most expensive chip in the mod — worth every singularity.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOg.name=§c§lThe Singularity Chain
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOg.desc=Chapter five: the endgame. Three singularity machines entangle steam into singularities, a drilling hub runs remote mining armies, a matter aggregator prints ores from thin air, and the mineral cluster closes the book.%n%nThe chain: SSE → Steam Entangled Singularity → DSM dense steam → CSC → Critical Singularity → chips, remote nodes, the aggregator and the cluster.%n%nBring a big steam budget. You will need it.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOw.name=Entangle This
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAOw.desc=The Steam Singularity Entangler is the singularity factory: a 24x30x23 steel structure that swallows the highest grade of plain steam in its input hatches, once per second, all of it.%n%nHeat accumulates as coefficient × 0.005 × x/(x+200,000) per cycle, where x is the liters swallowed this cycle; coefficients are 0.5 plain / 1.0 superheated / 2.0 supercritical.%n%nAt 100%% heat it resets and produces exactly 1 Steam Entangled Singularity. No power, no cooling hatch — just steam, endlessly.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPA.name=Heat Math
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPA.desc=The saturation curve means diminishing returns: at 200,000 L per cycle you reach half of the per-cycle ceiling (0.5%%), and throwing 10x more steam never buys 10x the heat.%n%nIdle or steam-starved machines bleed 1%% heat per second — keep the entangler fed or the bar walks backwards.%n%nOutput is checked against output bus space before spawning: a full bus pauses production instead of voiding your singularity.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPQ.name=A Thousand to One
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPQ.desc=The Dense State Manipulator compresses plain steam into dense steam at 1000:1 — and decompresses back at 1:1000. Screwdriver toggles the mode.%n%nIt eats whichever grade sits in its input hatches (steam / superheated / supercritical) and emits the matching dense variant as an accumulating real-number stream.%n%nThe structure is a 21x30x11 tier-2 rhodium-plated palladium build — the same family as the CSC.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPg.name=Two Kinds of Fuel
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPg.desc=The DSM runs on singularity fuel from its input bus: a plain singularity gives 200 seconds but takes a 20%% output haircut; a critical singularity gives the same 200 seconds with zero loss.%n%nFuel is consumed only while working — shutdowns keep counting down but eat nothing. When the timer hits zero it auto-refills from the bus.%n%nFeed it criticals once your CSC is online. That 20%% adds up fast at million-liter scale.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPw.name=Critical Mass
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAPw.desc=The Critical Singularity Compressor is the SSE's bigger sibling: 27x27x21 of rhodium-plated palladium, and it only accepts dense steam variants — dense steam, dense superheated, dense supercritical.%n%nIts saturation curve is far friendlier: 0.005 × x/(x+5,000) per cycle. A modest dense stream fills the bar dramatically faster than the SSE ever could.%n%nAt 100%% heat: 1 Critical Steam Entangled Singularity. Handle with respect — dropped criticals detonate after 3 seconds.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQA.name=The Critical Singularity
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQA.desc=Hold the endgame currency. Critical singularities buy the biggest toys: the Cycle Overlimit Chip (64 of them), reinforced hub chip bills, lossless DSM fuel, and turbine singularity mode 2 (5x output).%n%nMind the drop behavior: 3 seconds after touching the ground it explodes — 50%% TNT block damage, 20x TNT entity damage — and scatters 4-12 plain singularities with their own 4-10 second fuses.%n%nKeep them in inventory or machines. Never in item form on the floor.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQQ.name=Cycle Past the Limit
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQQ.desc=The Steam Turbine Cycle Overlimit Chip goes into the mega turbine and lifts the output-side conversion factor — same steam, more EU.%n%nThe assembler bill is endgame-grade: 64 any-UV circuits, 32 compact fusion coils, 64 critical singularities, 32 field generators VIII, 64 ZPM electric pumps and 1,000mB of organics — a 600-second IV cook.%n%nWith it active, superheated and supercritical grades condense to distilled water as well.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQg.name=The Drilling Hub
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQg.desc=The Singularity Drilling Hub is a 12x12x12 steel cube that drives remote worker nodes: singularity miner nodes mine ores, drilling nodes pull underground fluids — outputs land in the hub's buses and hatches.%n%nIt demands superheated steam — 8,000 L/s base plus each active working node's tier cost — and gets no 4x speedup from it.%n%nThe assembler controller recipe runs 16 singularities. No chip required for binding.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQw.name=Nodes Go Remote
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAQw.desc=The two worker nodes, one of each please. Miner node: 64x64 area, fortune VI, 4-second cycles, 5,000 L/s — upgradable through four tiers to 288x288, fortune X, 10-tick cycles, 240,000 L/s. Drilling node: 1x1 chunk extraction at factor 10, up to 8x8 at factor 18.%n%nEach binds for 1 singularity; upgrades happen in the node GUI or the hub terminal using drill controllers plus 16/32/64 (256 for miner tier IV) singularities.%n%nBound nodes chunk-load themselves and their work area automatically.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAARA.name=Matter From the Crust
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAARA.desc=The Crust Matter Aggregator is the endgame void miner: 26x26x8, fed by a runaway singularity node in its structure, 24,000 L/s of steam in any of three grades (dense steam needs just 240 L/s).%n%nOre modes 0/1/2 (raw / fortune-rolled rich raw / crushed at 1.5x), fortune III through XV, directional mode with a 1 + 2500%%/lowest-3-weights multiplier, and dimension display items to mine other worlds from your living room.%n%nConfigure everything from the terminal GUI — screwdriver-free.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAARQ.name=The Full Cluster
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAARQ.desc=The Steam Mineral Logistics Cluster is GTSR's final machine: a 15x20x29 main hall (plus 8-deep extension segments) hosting one controller, seven processing units (crusher, ore washer, centrifuge, thermal centrifuge, sifter, magnetic separator, furnace), five amplifier units and a logistics unit.%n%nPreheat costs 2,000 L/s steam + 10 L/s lubricant; every processing chain drinks 8,000 × 1.5^(chain length - 1) L/s.%n%nOre in, products out, entire chains executed atomically. The full mineral pipeline under one roof.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAARg.name=§4§lChallenges
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAARg.desc=Six stretch goals for the steam barons. All are checkbox tasks — the quest book trusts your honor.%n%nSafe critical transport, 300%%+ turbine efficiency, cross-dimensional commuting, drilling hub steam budgeting, cluster amplifier tuning, and custom singularity events.%n%nSingularities rain on completion.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAARw.name=Handle With Care
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAARw.desc=Move a Critical Steam Entangled Singularity from its CSC to a machine that consumes one — without it ever touching the ground as an item.%n%nThe rules: 3 seconds after landing it detonates (50%% TNT block damage, 20x TNT entity damage) and scatters 4-12 plain singularities on 4-10 second fuses. Plain singularities pop after 5 seconds too — 2x TNT entity damage, no block damage.%n%nDirect inventory-to-machine transfers only. No droppers, no death-drop courier runs.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAASA.name=Three Hundred Percent
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAASA.desc=Build a mega turbine that sustains over 300%% efficiency. Dense supercritical steam alone caps at 300%% — you need stack bonuses on top: 4 stack groups (+40%% ceiling), tungsten steel pipes (+25%%), high-tier casings (+5%% per tier) or singularity mode (+100%%).%n%nFeed it dense supercritical from a DSM chain — every liter of dense steam is a thousand liters of plain steam in disguise.%n%nScreenshot the efficiency bar. Frame it.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAASQ.name=Dimension Hopper
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAASQ.desc=Use the hub terminal's teleport button to cross dimensions: a node placed in the Nether (or any modded dimension), teleported to from your Overworld hub.%n%nThe teleport handles cross-dimension transfer automatically — chunk loading, mount dismounting, safe landing scan — for exactly 1 singularity.%n%nThe range check still applies: you must be within 8 blocks of the hub controller when clicking.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAASg.name=Steam Bill Math
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAASg.desc=Run a drilling hub with at least three working nodes at once and compute your bill: 8,000 L/s base plus every active node's tier cost — drillers 2K/6K/12K/20K, miners 5K/10K/20K/80K/240K by tier.%n%nA tier-3 driller plus two tier-2 miners = 8,000 + 12,000 + 20,000 + 20,000 = 60,000 L/s of superheated steam, minimum.%n%nIdle nodes cost nothing — only actively working ones draw steam. Throttle smart.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAASw.name=Booster Buffet
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAASw.desc=Tune all five cluster amplifiers on one cluster and balance the books. Each running amplifier costs fluid by its tier — 4/8/12/16 L/s — and applies its multiplier to the steam bill: parallel ×1.3, speed ×1.4, primary output ×2.0, secondary output ×1.6, steam saver ×1.1.%n%nPrimary output boosts take only the highest of their kind; secondary boosts add up; steam savings cap at 48%% total.%n%nThe question every cluster engineer answers differently: how much parallel can you afford?
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAATA.name=Singularity, Custom Order
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAATA.desc=Spawn a custom runaway singularity with the admin command: /gtsr singularity <range> <speed> <damage> <duration|NA> <special> [color] [fxRadius].%n%nSpecial modes: null (full behavior), onlypull (pulls but never absorbs), nature (harmless, harvestable), nullplus. Sixteen dye colors for the core.%n%nThe config file tunes natural spawn frequency (singularitySpawnFrequency, default 48) and can disable block destruction entirely (singularityDestroyBlocks).
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAATQ.name=§b§lBeyond Steam
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAATQ.desc=GTSR is one third of the MIAO family. The other two mods — and the quest line that ties them together — wait beyond this chapter.%n%nA quick look at what each adds and how they slot into a GTNH pack alongside this line. No tasks from them appear here; their own quest lines ship with them.%n%nInstall order never matters: they are all independent mods.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAATg.name=Cut the Cables
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAATg.desc=GT-Simple-Wireless-Network (GTSWN) lays a wireless EU layer over GregTech: a wireless energy monitor, a pocket HUD, link terminals that attach virtual-cable covers to any machine, wall-sized info panels and a quantum extension for ME networks.%n%nEverything is LV-era friendly and pairs naturally with GTSR's steam turbines — the turbine makes the EU, GTSWN moves it without a single cable.%n%nInstall it and its quest line appears alongside this one.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAATw.name=Something Interesting
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAATw.desc=GT-Interesting-Thing (GTIT) is the fun drawer of the family: novelty items, toys, and its own neko coin economy.%n%nLight-hearted by design — none of it gates your tech tree, all of it brightens the grind.%n%nAnother independent mod with its own BetterQuesting line when installed.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUA.name=The MIAO Verse
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUA.desc=MIAO-GTNH is the glue: a quest-and-content layer that ties GTSR, GTSWN and GTIT together into one storyline.%n%nWith all three installed, the MIAO line picks up where this one ends — crossover quests, shared milestones, and the full steam-to-wireless-to-whimsy arc.%n%nThat's the graduation path. Finish this line first; the verse will wait.
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUQ.name=Graduation Day
betterquesting.quest.R1RTUgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAUQ.desc=You built all 22 multiblocks, chained three singularity machines, wired a hub network across dimensions and ran a mineral cluster on steam alone.%n%nThe final checkbox of the GTSR line. Claim the diploma — a fistful of singularities and the satisfaction of a steam age done right.%n%nNext stop: GTSWN, GTIT, and the MIAO verse beyond.
# BQ quests END
